WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:00.930
- Let's finish out
(audience applauding)

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:03.540
with one last story I found
on the pages of social media.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:04.728
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:04.728 --> 00:00:07.282
(audience cheering)
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.282 --> 00:00:08.115
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.115 --> 00:00:10.050
All right, as we've talked
about much of this hour,

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.120
it can be difficult
for people in the trans

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.240
and non-gender-conforming
community to find safe spaces

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.400
to just kick back and be themselves.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.890
That is one reason a
Brooklyn athlete decided

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.880
to open OutBox, a boxing gym
designed as an inclusive place

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.790
for anyone and everyone
looking for a good workout,

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.450
but particularly those
who identify as LGBTQ+.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.860
We have him on the line right now,

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.480
watching on "NBC 4 New York."

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.339
Let's welcome Max, everybody.

00:00:35.339 --> 00:00:36.420
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.988
- Hi, Kelly.
- What's up, Max?

00:00:38.988 --> 00:00:39.975
- Hi. (chuckles)

00:00:39.975 --> 00:00:40.808
Thanks-
- Oh, my God.

00:00:40.808 --> 00:00:42.060
I love all the colorful gloves.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.770
I'm so into it.
- Oh, yeah.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.415
Kelly, we're a gay gym here, come on.

00:00:45.415 --> 00:00:46.248
(audience laughing)

00:00:46.248 --> 00:00:47.460
- All right, I love it, I love it.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.740
So explain the gym to everyone.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.140
- All right, well, we're
a trans-owned boxing gym

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.570
that centers the LGBTQ+ community,

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.330
particularly our trans
and non-binary members.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.280
Our gym is completely non-gendered.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.700
Everything from your first
experience at the front desk,

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.140
the bathrooms, locker rooms,

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.000
the language our instructors use,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.880
we take gender out of everything.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.530
I think that is a huge part

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.470
that keeps people out of the
gym, especially trans folks.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:17.280
And all of our trainers are
queer, which I'm proud to say.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.030
And we've become way more than just a gym.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.560
We've become a community space.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.290
We've had drag shows, we've had parties,

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:28.320
we've had karaoke nights,
blasting "Since U Been Gone."

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.332
- Yes.

00:01:29.332 --> 00:01:30.165
(audience cheering)

00:01:30.165 --> 00:01:32.220
- So we have a special space here, so.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.630
- Well, okay, so this idea came

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.190
from personal experience, right?

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:36.510
- It did, yes.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:41.510
I was a competitive boxer
and I was about to go pro.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:45.090
And the only problem is that
I was in the female division.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.520
And I knew my whole life I was trans.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.320
I just picked boxing over my happiness

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.140
for almost 30 years of my life.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.700
After the pandemic happened,

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.250
like many, many trans people, honestly,

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.560
I was like, now is the time.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.210
Everything's closed.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:04.020
And I decided that I need
to do something for myself,

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:07.620
and I transitioned, and
that's when I realized,

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.730
wow, gyms and sports are
really uncomfortable spaces

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.950
and they don't want us here.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.650
So during the pandemic
when everything was closed,

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.580
I decided to start hosting
LGBTQ+ boxing classes

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:21.720
in the park.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.340
And week after week after week,

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.990
they were not only selling out,

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.910
there was people coming
out of the woodwork,

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.880
like more people week after week.

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:33.210
So I was like, I think
there's a huge need for this.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:34.560
And that's when OutBox was born.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.930
We opened up a brick-and-mortar
gym in Brooklyn

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.910
and we've been going ever since.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.137
- Well, congratulations.
(audience applauding)

00:02:41.137 --> 00:02:43.620
It's incredible what you did for yourself

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:44.580
and what you're doing for others.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:45.750
Thank you so much, Max.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.400
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.350
- Oh, thank.
(bell ringing)

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.487
Oh. (laughs)

00:02:49.487 --> 00:02:50.580
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.413
- And that's not all.

00:02:51.413 --> 00:02:54.060
Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.920
the go-to pen at "The
Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.920
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.840
So they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:01.673
How's that sound?

00:03:01.673 --> 00:03:02.522
- Wow.
(audience applauding)

00:03:02.522 --> 00:03:03.840
- Oh.
(audience cheering)

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:04.673
That's awesome.

00:03:04.673 --> 00:03:06.090
I did not know that.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:07.061
Thank you.
- Absolutely.

00:03:07.061 --> 00:03:07.987
Have a good one, Max.
(audience cheering)

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:10.529
Thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:03:10.529 --> 00:03:11.825
Patricia Clarkson,
(audience cheering)

00:03:11.825 --> 00:03:16.213
Trace Lysette, Laverne Cox,
Jeff, Harley, and Kira.

00:03:16.213 --> 00:03:17.046
Y'all have a great day.

00:03:17.046 --> 00:03:18.754
And if it's not, try and change it.

